## Test Smell Audit — Academic 19-Smell Catalog (testsmells.org)

**Target:** `DataAccess.IntegrationTests/UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`  
**Framework:** MSTest 4.1 (.NET 10)  
**Integration calibration:** Applied — class is marked `[TestCategory("Integration")]`

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 2           | 2              |
| Medium   | 2           | 2              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test)

**Affected:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
    // ← No assertion — passes even if all inserts silently fail
}
```

**Fix:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — 100% pass rate even if insertion is completely broken.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic

**Affected:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 94)

```csharp
var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);   // path A
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);       // path B
}
```

**Problem:** Only one branch ever executes per run. If the type hierarchy changes, the "wrong" branch silently passes. Hidden test gap.

**Fix:** Write two explicit tests:
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenStandard_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenPremium_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("vip@example.com", "Vip", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("vip@example.com") as PremiumUser;

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** One code path is permanently untested — regressions are invisible.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Sleepy Test

**Affected:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);  // hard-coded 3-second wait
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Note:** Downgraded from High because this is an integration test — async coordination delays are sometimes necessary. Still a smell because `Thread.Sleep` is both slow and non-deterministic (3 s may not be enough on slow CI; always wastes 3 s even when the event fires in 50 ms).

**Fix:** Use a polling/retry helper:
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var sent = await WaitUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));

    Assert.IsTrue(sent, "Notification was not sent within timeout.");
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky failures in CI + unnecessarily slow suite.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette

**Affected:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
// 4 assertions, zero explanation messages
```

**Problem:** When one fails, the MSTest runner shows only "Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<Alice>. Actual:<null>." — no context about *which property* was being verified or why.

**Fix:** Add message parameters:
```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should persist");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should persist");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Id should be auto-assigned on insert");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slow failure diagnosis; developers must open code to understand which property failed.

---

### Smell-Free Patterns ✅

The following tests are well-structured — good examples for the team:

| Test | Why It's Good |
|------|---------------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange/act/assert, focused on one behavior |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single concern, meaningful assertion |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count is contextually obvious (3 inserts → expect 3), uses `CollectionAssert` |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Good concurrency test, clear assertion |

The in-memory SQLite setup (`Data Source=:memory:`) is **not** a Mystery Guest — it's explicit, hermetic, and doesn't depend on external state. Well done.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix Effort | Impact |
|----------|-------|-----------|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test (`BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors`) | ~2 min | Eliminates a false-pass test |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic (`GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType`) | ~10 min | Closes a hidden coverage gap |
| 3 | Sleepy Test (`NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay`) | ~15 min | Reduces flakiness + speeds CI |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette (`InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase`) | ~3 min | Faster failure diagnosis |

**Bottom line:** 4 of 8 tests are clean. The two High-severity findings (#1 and #2) represent real testing gaps where bugs could ship undetected. Fix those first.
